{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979987-quick-and-dirty-pathless","id":979987,"title":"Quick and dirty Pathless","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-01T18:40:34-07:00","id":979987,"title":"Quick and dirty Pathless","content":"Question: What would be the simplest way to make Pathless Mages a thing in Mage, not as the default but as a minority compared to Mages with Paths. I'm fighting the simplest most basic way is to just say &quot;choose a good concept/philosophy and pick two Arcana&quot;, but there're a few more things from there. For example, would it be a good restriction to say that one of the two has to be subtle and one of them has to be gross? And how would Mage Sight work out? Does it need more than just asking the player to come up with something?<br /> <br /> Obviously, there are also lore and roleplaying considerations, but that's always been easier than mechanics for me. I'd have it be that there's a suspicion that Pathless are less stable and more likely to become Scelesti or Banishers, but I'm not sure if this should be true. I'd probably not have it be big enough to make a social impact, maybe a situation where the ST would rule that there's a penalty for making a social role with someone who distrusts the Pathless. I might also say that Gifted Scientists are more likely to be Pathless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T18:49:16-07:00","id":979990,"title":"","content":"You could have them awaken with neither Ruling nor Inferior arcana, and simply treat everything as Common. Let them spend their arcana dots however they want as long as it respects the base Gnosis limitations (probably not counting increased Wisdom from sacrificing merit dots).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T19:27:59-07:00","id":980010,"title":"","content":"Nah, I really want to stick with them having Ruling and Inferior Arcana. This is meant to allow character concepts that don't fit in with the existing pairs. For example, an immortality-seeking neurosurgeon with Life/Mind. Or a botanist warlock with Life/Fate. Or an animist with Matter/Spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T19:51:30-07:00","id":980019,"title":"","content":"You might find some help in the Mage Translation Guide. It's couched in Ascension terms, but it provides an interesting way of doing Ruling/Inferior Arcana without (quite) Paths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T20:02:50-07:00","id":980024,"title":"","content":"If you keep Ruling and Inferior arcana then even with all possible variations it's pretty much inevitable that Mages would develop terminology to refer to it and you would still be stuck with Paths, just a whole lot more of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T20:46:41-07:00","id":980039,"title":"","content":"Well, it's not that common of phenomenon, but I might say that Pathless Mages sometimes make up Paths for themselves. The Pathless awaken to fragments multiple watchtowers, a distorted version of a watchtower, or manage to carve their own foothold somewhere in the Supernal. There are still the five core paths and realms, it's just that the Pathless end up perceiving them in highly irregular ways compared to other Mages. Each one experiences it differently- one Pathless might perceive their Awakening as being caught between Stygia and Arcadia, leading to them having the Arcana of Time and Death. It's wildly unlikely that this person would meet another Pathless with the same combination of Arcana and the same perception of how they gained them, so it's very unlikely that any long term perception of a new path would form.<br /> <br /> To give another example, the Life/Mind Mage Awakened to the Primal Wild, but perceived it in an altered way based on her paradigm that completely rejected the animistic and spiritual aspects of the realm, instead perceiving the platonic ideal of nature that it represents as arising from the union of mind and body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-01-2016, 11:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T21:28:28-07:00","id":980066,"title":"","content":"It would have to be -exceedingly- rare to avoid recorded repeats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T21:42:21-07:00","id":980072,"title":"","content":"Record repeats is a bit of a loaded thing, because Joe Awakened can't just open The Encyclopedia Arcane for a list of every Mage, their ruling Arcana, and how they experienced their Awakening. <br /> <br /> There could be ten Mages active at once who all had the same ruling Arcana and Awakening as Craniac the Undying (though that's way more than I'd imagine), and each one could easily have no idea that the other nine existed.<br /> <br /> But this isn't really helping flesh out the idea, so let's move on to working out how Mage Sight would work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T21:45:12-07:00","id":980074,"title":"","content":"My point is simply that with the obsession Mages have for taxonomy it's unlikely that such anomalies would go unnoticed and without an attempt at classification and searching out of patterns of re-occurrence. By all means, carry on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T22:01:50-07:00","id":980084,"title":"","content":"Normally the game would achieve such groupings through Legacies. However if you want, and intend it to be rare and little understood, you could fall back on the idea of unknown Watch Towers. That would make the characters mysteries in their own right and if desired there could be recorded examples of ancient Mages who Awakened to the same tower.<br /> \u200bIf you don't want to break too far away from the other Paths you would still have a subtle/gross pairing and as for Mage Sight, it would be based on your Arcanum. For example, your Life/Mind Mage might view everything as living organisms, ruled by natural processes like living machines. Think L.Ron Hubbard only with magic making anything real and possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T22:06:08-07:00","id":980087,"title":"","content":"If you have two Ruling Arcana, Mage Sight doesn't need to change. Active Sight turns on your two Ruling Arcana as normal. So that part's easy enough.<br /> <br /> Some caveats: if a mage dramatically fails a Scrutiny roll, they draw the attention of &quot;a Supernal being of the mage's Path.&quot; What beings are Pathless mages drawn to? One option would just be the individual entities of their Ruling Arcana, like the Life/Mind mage would be drawn to Atavisms and Wraiths. That would have implications for Supernal summoning, too.<br /> <br /> What can they use as Path tools? That's going to have direct mechanical implications for yantras<br /> <br /> If they create a Demesne, will it just grant bonuses to their two Ruling Arcana?<br /> <br /> I can't think of anything that would break if you had two Gross or Subtle Ruling Arcana.<br /> <br /> I'm trying to think of other stuff that's <i>mechanically</i> affected by Path itself. It might have implications for what Legacies they can join? But most Legacies aren't restricted to Path alone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T22:18:53-07:00","id":980098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979987-quick-and-dirty-pathless?p=980087#post980087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have two Ruling Arcana, Mage Sight doesn't need to change. Active Sight turns on your two Ruling Arcana as normal. So that part's easy enough.<br /> <br /> Some caveats: if a mage dramatically fails a Scrutiny roll, they draw the attention of &amp;quot;a Supernal being of the mage's Path.&amp;quot; What beings are Pathless mages drawn to? One option would just be the individual entities of their Ruling Arcana, like the Life/Mind mage would be drawn to Atavisms and Wraiths. That would have implications for Supernal summoning, too.<br /> <br /> What can they use as Path tools? That's going to have direct mechanical implications for yantras<br /> <br /> If they create a Demesne, will it just grant bonuses to their two Ruling Arcana?<br /> <br /> I can't think of anything that would break if you had two Gross or Subtle Ruling Arcana.<br /> <br /> I'm trying to think of other stuff that's <i>mechanically</i> affected by Path itself. It might have implications for what Legacies they can join? But most Legacies aren't restricted to Path alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's all pretty good. <br /> <br /> About Path tools, does it break anything or wreck the balance if you just tell the player &quot;pick Tools that make sense for the character&quot;? <br /> <br /> I'd be fine saying that a Pathless Mage can't join Path-specific legacies. There are plenty of non-Path-specific ones, so it isn't really a huge hindrance. Pathless are meant to be kind of weirdos compared to other mages, so I think it'd work. <br /> <br /> I'd say the answers to all your other questions would be yes, like the Supernal entities and Demesne stuff. About two Gross or two Subtle, I guess it wouldn't be unbalanced. I was mostly keeping the Gross and Subtle combo for tradition, but I suppose I could break with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T22:19:16-07:00","id":980100,"title":"","content":"Why come up with a thing called Pathless? Just let people make up their own Path and go from there. If you're good enough to come up with something coherent, there's no reason not to run with it, no matter what set of Ruling/Inferior Arcana they justify with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T22:40:51-07:00","id":980109,"title":"","content":"I think you're fine letting players pick their own &quot;Path&quot; tools. I would suggest having them look at the suggestions on page 121 for inspiration, just to keep them conceptually distinct from say, Order Tools.<br /> <br /> You know what you could do? To emphasize the Pathless distinction and the idea of claiming your own access to the Supernal, don't let them use the Path tools category at all. Instead, give them 1 free dot in Shadow Name and have them come up with their own personal symbols and tools.<br /> <br /> This is kind of making me want to create a Pathless, Nameless mage lurking in the shadows with a bunch of dots in Shadow Name and Mystery Cult Initiation and Occultation...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979987-quick-and-dirty-pathless?p=980100#post980100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why come up with a thing called Pathless? Just let people make up their own Path and go from there. If you're good enough to come up with something coherent, there's no reason not to run with it, no matter what set of Ruling/Inferior Arcana they justify with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they find this possibility more interesting, presumably.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 10-02-2016, 01:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T22:42:09-07:00","id":980110,"title":"","content":"The concept of the Pathless is a way to fit them into existing Mage canon with as little disruption as possible. So, basically, it's saying: &quot;these are the five paths, but sometimes someone doesn't Awaken conventionally and they end up having a different outlook and Arcana combination&quot;.<br /> <br /> Running with homebrew too far means you have to disregard and ignore more and more of the existing content. The problem with making Geckopirateship's Dream Game is that Onyx Path doesn't support Geckopirateship's Dream Game or release content for it, and people on this forum don't play or discuss Geckopirateship's Dream Game.<br /> <br /> Also, while the MCG says that Enlightened Scientists don't have paths, I'd prefer to blur the divide between them and &quot;regular&quot; mages, and part of the way to do that is to give them Paths, but say that they're slightly more likely to be Pathless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T17:53:15-07:00","id":981144,"title":"","content":"Hm, maybe I'll make three types. Irregulars, who Awaken to one of the five realms but perceive it in a way other than the norm, Betweeners, who Awaken to fragments of two realms simultaneously, and Twisted, who Awaken to something too chaotic and warped to be identified with any existing realms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T08:13:27-07:00","id":981448,"title":"","content":"Doesnt the 1ed book Mage Chronicler's Guide has a section on both pathless mages and magic as science?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}